  "34": {
    "class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
    "inputs": {
      "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is the source video and provides the original performance, setting, camera work, and soundtrack.\n<Picture 1> is the three-view face reference for <Subject 1>. It is the sole reference for facial identity, face shape, facial features, and makeup. It also shows the hairstyle and the details of visible head accessories.\n<Picture 2> is the face-masked three-view full-body reference for the same <Subject 1> in the same styling. It defines the body shape, head-to-body proportions, clothing, footwear, and accessories. It also shows the full hair length, the hairstyle from behind, and how the hair falls over the outfit.\n<Subject 1> is the single character who takes the place of the original main performer in <Video 1>.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing + character replacement] <Subject 1> performs the original actions with the same timing as the main performer in <Video 1>. The setting, background, framing, camera movement, and soundtrack follow the source.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Video 1> (source video editing): fully_preserved - the original performance, poses, movement path, timing, setting, props, lighting, camera work, and soundtrack. The main performer’s appearance is replaced by <Subject 1>.\n<Picture 1>: reference - facial identity, face shape, facial features, makeup, hairstyle, and visible head accessory details.\n<Picture 2>: reference - body shape, head-to-body proportions, clothing, footwear, accessory placement, and the full hairstyle in relation to the outfit.\n<Subject 1>: fully_preserved - one consistent identity and styling throughout the clip, with an uncovered face matching <Picture 1>.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] From 00:00.000 through the end of the clip, <Subject 1> follows the original performer’s poses, gestures, movement path, and timing. Whenever the face comes into view, it is uncovered and matches the identity, features, and makeup in <Picture 1>. The hairstyle follows both references, including the hair length and how it falls over the clothing. The body proportions, outfit, shoes, and accessories match <Picture 2> as they come into view. The background, props, framing, and camera movement follow <Video 1>.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe original soundtrack from <Video 1> plays throughout in sync with the action.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nNo additional music. Any music in the source soundtrack is retained."
    },
